return {h=10,w=1050,cr=120,hc=15,bh=70,gr="medium-slow",eg={"mineral"},st={55,95,115,45,45,35},ab={{69,0},{5,0},{8,1}},genus={en="Rock Pokémon",es="Pokémon Roca",pt="Pokémon Rocha"},flavor={en={[1]="Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.",[2]="Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.",[3]="Often seen rolling down mountain trails. Obstacles are just things to roll straight over, not avoid.",[4]="With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn't mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.",[5]="A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path.",[6]="It travels by rolling on mountain paths. If it gains too much speed, it stops by running into huge rocks.",[7]="GRAVELER grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This Pokémon eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis.",[8]="Rocks are GRAVELER’s favorite food. This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom.",[9]="They descend from mountains by tumbling down steep slopes. They are so brutal, they smash aside obstructing trees and massive boulders with thunderous tackles.",[10]="Be careful while hiking on mountain trails. GRAVELER may come rolling down the path without slowing.",[11]="Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.",[12]="GRAVELER make their homes on sheer cliff faces by gouging out numerous horizontal holes.",[13]="It tumbles down slopes, heedless of any body parts chipping off. It eats a ton of rocks daily.",[14]="It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.",[15]="With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn’t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.",[16]="A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path.",[17]="It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.",[18]="It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.",[21]="It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.",[22]="It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.",[23]="With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn’t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.",[24]="Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.",[25]="Graveler grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This Pokémon eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis.",[26]="Rocks are Graveler’s favorite food. This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom.",[27]="Mossy rocks are its favorite food. It can devour a ton a day while crunching loudly.",[28]="This slow-footed Pokémon moves by curling up and rolling instead of walking. With enough momentum, its speed can exceed 60 mph.",[29]="It climbs up cliffs as it heads toward the peak of a mountain. As soon as it reaches the summit, it rolls back down the way it came.",[30]="It travels by rolling down cliffs. If it falls into a river, it will explode with its last gasp.",[31]="Often seen rolling down mountain trails. Obstacles are just things to roll straight over, not avoid.",[32]="Often seen rolling down mountain trails. Obstacles are just things to roll straight over, not avoid.",[39]="Dwells in holes dug into sheer walls of stone. It enjoys rolling down slopes as though it were a boulder during a rockfall, so keep an eye upward while traversing mountain roads."},es={[23]="De naturaleza descuidada y libre, no le importa dañarse cuando baja rodando montañas.",[24]="Se mueve rodando cuesta abajo y sobre cualquier obstáculo, sin frenar ni cambiar de dirección.",[25]="Graveler crece alimentándose a base de piedras. Y, según parece, las prefiere cubiertas de musgo. Cada día se abre camino comiéndose una tonelada de rocas.",[26]="Las piedras son la comida preferida de Graveler. Este Pokémon sube a la cima de las montañas devorando todas las rocas que va encontrando a su paso. Una vez que alcanza la cumbre, baja rodando hasta la falda.",[27]="Su comida preferida son las rocas cubiertas de musgo. Llega a comer más de una tonelada en un día y causa un gran estruendo al masticar.",[28]="Se desplaza rodando, pues a pie va muy despacio. Si toma carrerilla, puede superar los 100 km/h.",[29]="Escala los riscos de las montañas y, una vez alcanzada la cima, desciende rodando por los senderos.",[30]="Se desplaza rodando por las laderas. Si por mala fortuna termina cayendo en un río, con su último aliento causa una gigantesca explosión.",[31]="Se le suele ver rodando montaña abajo. No evita los obstáculos, sino que los arrolla.",[32]="Se le suele ver rodando montaña abajo. No evita los obstáculos, sino que los arrolla."},pt="Mora em buracos cavados em paredões de pedra. Gosta de rolar ladeira abaixo como uma pedra em um deslizamento, então fique de olho no alto ao passar por trilhas nas montanhas."},evo={{s=74},{s=75,from=74,c={{t="level-up",lv=25}}},{s=76,from=75,c={{t="trade"}}}},moves={[1]={1,33,1,111,11,111,16,88,21,120,29,106,36,89,43,153},[2]={1,33,1,111,11,111,16,88,21,120,29,106,36,89,43,153},[3]={1,33,1,111,1,88,6,111,11,88,16,222,21,120,27,106,34,205,41,89,48,153},[4]={1,33,1,111,1,88,6,111,11,88,16,222,21,120,27,106,34,205,41,89,48,153},[5]={1,33,1,111,1,300,1,88,6,300,11,88,16,222,21,120,29,205,37,350,45,89,53,153,62,38},[6]={1,33,1,111,1,300,1,88,6,300,11,88,16,222,21,120,29,205,37,350,45,89,53,153,62,38},[